title: Status
new-page: true
is-special: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.inflation_2 = Q.inflation ? Q.inflation.toFixed(1) : '0';
Q.unemployment_2 = Q.unemployment ? Q.unemployment.toFixed(1) : '0';
Q.economic_growth_2 = Q.economic_growth ? Q.economic_growth.toFixed(1) : '0';
Q.dissent_disp = Math.round(Q.dissent_percent || 0);
Q.budget_disp = Math.round(Q.budget * 10) / 10;
Q.interest_rate_disp = Math.round(Q.interest_rate * 10) / 10;
Q.thatcher_rating_disp = Math.round(Q.thatcher_rating);
Q.lab_leader_rating_disp = Math.round(Q.lab_leader_rating);
!}

= Status

[+ month : month +] [+ year +]

Resources: [+ resources +]

Conservative position: [? if con_in_government : in government ?][? if not con_in_government : Opposition ?]

Party dissent: [+ dissent_disp : dissent +]

Your rating: [+ thatcher_rating : rating +] ([+ thatcher_rating_disp +])

Labour leader ([+ lab_leader +]): [+ lab_leader_rating : rating +] ([+ lab_leader_rating_disp +])

= Government

Prime Minister: [+ prime_minister +] ([+ pm_party +])

[? if lib_lab_pact : The Lib-Lab Pact is in force. ?]

[? if con_in_government : Chancellor: [+ chancellor +]. Employment: [+ employment_secretary +]. Industry: [+ industry_secretary +]. ?]

[? if con_in_government : Cabinet: [+ cabinet_dry +]% dry. Backbench rebellion: [+ rebellion_disp +]/10. ?][? if con_in_government and cabinet_dry < 60 : Cabinet revolt: [+ cabinet_revolt_disp +]/10. ?][? if govt_type >= 2 and con_in_government : Partners' discontent: [+ partner_dissent_disp +]/10. ?]

House of Commons ([+ total_seats +] seats, [+ majority_line +] for a majority):

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Conservative and Unionist Party">Conservative</span>!}: [+ con_mps +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Labour Party">Labour</span>!}: [+ lab_mps +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Liberals, and the SDP once it is founded">!}[+ lib_name +]{!</span>!}: [+ lib_mps +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Scottish National Party">SNP</span>!}: [+ snp_mps +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Plaid Cymru">Plaid Cymru</span>!}: [+ pc_mps +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Ulster Unionists, SDLP and Northern Irish independents">Northern Ireland</span>!}: [+ ni_mps +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The Speaker, the Scottish Labour Party and vacancies">Others</span>!}: [+ other_mps +]

Next election: [? if election_called : [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +] ?][? if not election_called : due by [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +] ?]

= Economy

Inflation: [+ inflation_2 +]%

Unemployment: [+ unemployment_2 +]%

Growth: [+ economic_growth_2 +]%

[? if not con_in_government : Pay norm: [+ pay_norm +]% ?]

[? if con_in_government : Bank Rate: [+ interest_rate_disp +]% ?]

[? if con_in_government : Budget: [+ budget_disp +] ?][? if con_in_government and budget < 0 : (borrowing) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Income tax: [+ basic_rate +]% basic, [+ top_rate +]% top. VAT: [+ vat +]% ?]

[? if con_in_government : Public spending: [+ spending : taxation +] ?]

@politics

[? if con_in_government : **The Cabinet** ([+ cabinet_dry +]% dry) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Chancellor: [+ chancellor +] ([+ chancellor_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Employment: [+ employment_secretary +] ([+ employment_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Industry: [+ industry_secretary +] ([+ industry_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Home Office: [+ home_secretary +] ([+ home_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Foreign Office: [+ foreign_secretary +] ([+ foreign_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Environment: [+ environment_secretary +] ([+ environment_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Defence: [+ defence_secretary +] ([+ defence_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Education: [+ education_secretary +] ([+ education_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : Health and Social Security: [+ health_secretary +] ([+ health_dry : drywet +]) ?]

[? if con_in_government : **Bills before Parliament** ?]

[? if con_in_government and bill_lines_n = 0 : None at present. ?]

[? if bill_lines_n >= 1 : [+ bill_line_1 +] ?]

[? if bill_lines_n >= 2 : [+ bill_line_2 +] ?]

[? if bill_lines_n >= 3 : [+ bill_line_3 +] ?]

[? if bill_lines_n >= 4 : [+ bill_line_4 +] ?]

[? if bill_lines_n >= 5 : [+ bill_line_5 +] ?]

[? if bill_lines_n >= 6 : [+ bill_line_6 +] ?]

[? if acts_n >= 1 : **Acts passed:** [+ acts_list +]. ?]


= Other Parties

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="David Steel's Liberals (and the SDP, once the Alliance forms)">!}[+ lib_name +]s{!</span>!}: [+ lib_relation : relationships +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Scottish National Party">SNP</span>!}: [+ snp_relation : relationships +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Plaid Cymru">Plaid Cymru</span>!}: [+ pc_relation : relationships +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The Ulster Unionists and their allies">Ulster Unionists</span>!}: [+ uup_relation : relationships +]

= Factions of the Conservative Party

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Free-market reformers: monetarism, lower taxes, curbing the unions. Keith Joseph, Geoffrey Howe.">Dries</span>!} strength: [+ dry_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ dry_dissent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="One Nation moderates who served under Heath and prefer consensus. Jim Prior, Ian Gilmour, Francis Pym.">Wets</span>!} strength: [+ wet_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ wet_dissent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Party managers who back whoever leads. Willie Whitelaw, Lord Carrington.">Loyalists</span>!} strength: [+ loyalist_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ loyalist_dissent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Traditionalists: law and order, immigration, the Union.">Right</span>!} strength: [+ right_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ right_dissent : dissent +]

Edward Heath: [? if heath_hostility >= 70 : openly hostile ?][? if heath_hostility >= 40 and heath_hostility < 70 : sulking ?][? if heath_hostility < 40 : grudgingly reconciled ?]

= Manifesto

[? if manifesto_planks = 0 : No policies adopted yet. ?][? if policy_monetarism : Sound money. ?] [? if policy_tax_cuts : Cut income tax. ?] [? if policy_union_reform : Trade union reform. ?] [? if policy_right_to_buy : Right to buy. ?] [? if policy_law_order : Law and order. ?] [? if policy_defence : Strong defence. ?] [? if policy_privatisation : Denationalisation. ?] [? if policy_immigration : Tighter immigration control. ?]

Devolution: [? if devolution_stance = 0 : opposed ?][? if devolution_stance = 1 : supported ?][? if devolution_stance = 2 : "No, for a better Bill" ?]

@industry
on-arrival: {!
Q.union_backlash_disp = Math.round(Q.union_backlash);
Q.economic_liberalism_disp = Math.round(Q.economic_liberalism);
Q.labour_credibility_disp = Math.round(Q.labour_credibility);
!}

= Industrial Relations

Strikes: [+ strike_wave : strikes +]

Public who say the unions have too much power: [+ union_backlash_disp +]%

Government pay norm: [+ pay_norm +]%

Our position on pay: [? if pay_stance = 0 : undecided ?][? if pay_stance = 1 : back the pay norm ?][? if pay_stance = 2 : free collective bargaining ?][? if pay_stance = 3 : statutory wage controls ?]

